# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/

# Testing / tooling caches
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Node / Vite / TypeScript
node_modules/
app/.tmp/
app/dist/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Screenshots of the running app, written by the CDP probes. Scratch: the
# Preview tab can serve them, and nothing in the product reads them.
#
# **The baseline captures are the exception, and they have to be.** Phase 0 of
# the workspace refine asked for five captures in `design-preview/` and none
# were ever taken; when the next pass went looking for the "before" state there
# was none, because this rule had kept the 4 October ones out of the repo too.
# A baseline that is not committed is not a baseline. The folder is ignored
# except for the captures the plan names and the two files that describe them.
# Phase 8's icon sheet is the same kind of exception: the weight table is
# argued from it, and a PNG nobody can open is not evidence.
design-preview/*
!design-preview/baseline/
!design-preview/icons-sheet.png
!design-preview/index.html
!design-preview/README.md

# The Rust shell, its build products and the frozen core all lived here. None of
# them exist any more: the window is `python -m tonyagent.window`, which reads
# app/dist/ off disk and runs the core from source. The entries below are kept
# only where something in the tree can still produce them.
#
#   app/src-tauri/target/, gen/, permissions/autogenerated/, binaries/
#   app/src-tauri/icons/android/, app/src-tauri/icons/ios/
#   scripts/build/            (PyInstaller's scratch, with the spec that used it)
#
# `app/icons/` is deliberately NOT ignored: those files are the window's icon
# now, they are read at runtime, and they are small.

# Local logs and scratch output
*.log
scripts/probe_*.jsonl
scripts/k2.py

# Leftover console capture from a build that failed loudly. Build output, not
# source: it is rewritten by the next build and nothing in the product reads it.
app/nt2.out

# The shortcut `scripts/make_shortcut.ps1` writes. It holds an absolute path to
# this checkout, so it is a fact about one machine and not about the project --
# run the script on a new machine rather than carrying the file over.
*.lnk

# Environment / secrets. API keys belong in the OS keyring, never on disk.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# The stray zero-byte files that used to live here (type names such as `dict`,
# `AsyncOpenAI`, `list[str]` created by mistyped shell redirects) were removed.
# They are deliberately NOT ignored any more: a future stray file should show up
# as untracked rather than be silently hidden by a name on this list.

# Freebuff's own project metadata
/.freebuff/

# PyInstaller intermediate output (the sidecar exe itself is ignored above)
build/
scripts/build/

# `tauri icon` also emits Android and iOS rasters. TONYAgent is desktop-only,
# so those are not regenerated or shipped.
app/src-tauri/icons/android/
app/src-tauri/icons/ios/
.shots/

# Probe outputs: the research scripts write these next to the repo, and they are
# readings rather than sources.
/.tmp-*

# An assistant's own working notes for this checkout: session memory and daily
# logs. Not part of the project, and not something a clone should inherit.
/.workbuddy-ai/
